          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:003527beb8fac5b7e20c0d0daca0f9d9248bbcb2f731c6e7610dd9a75979f370:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4adfdfb07b5546cab18da6811b734c8f",
      "statement": "Rebuilding the index is a function of the committed tree rather than a copy of unique state: `build_index` unlinks an existing database only once it holds the single-indexer lock and re-projects from a full walk of HEAD, while `reindex_isolated` builds the new database in a detached temp `git worktree` against its own state dir and installs it with an atomic `os.replace` under a brief live-lock, so long rebuilds never block narrow writers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/hypermnesic/index.py#L664-L711",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dfae9457c76941d21a0d03f7cf30b39394cf0a86bf4fb1ba10609d46e16d562f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/hypermnesic/index.py#L741-L769",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6947dde6b6b3cb015fdf5a246decc2a0c1f94cb2c136f39437ff01be80d56293:"
        },
        {
