    {
      "id": "claim_d3d74ea42dbf4284b726eb449ced4ea7",
      "statement": "A convergence pass is deliberately partial and non-blocking: it short-circuits within a debounce window before taking any lock, acquires the single-indexer `FileLock` non-blocking and serves the current projection on `LockBusyError`, does delta-replay plus a bounded dense fill (`CONVERGE_EMBED_BUDGET` chunks and doc surfaces per read), and signals `manual_reindex_recommended` instead of replaying whenever the delta exceeds `CONVERGE_MAX_DELTA_FILES`; it writes only the `.hypermnesic/` projection and never a full reindex or the repo.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/hypermnesic/config.py#L26-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:973f81c336d0f1d4a986f2fd83c203441cc24e18fe2641ab92b78719a7ccef8c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/hypermnesic/converge.py#L39-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:df55b8581d136095ad0860cfbc6924c3ce32b7017c85528211133c90eb3ac5be:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/hypermnesic/converge.py#L93-L176",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1867581a16c80e96833fe8812cc51c17d289de2e81c73ba8cf63a42ee16db4ab:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1a02da599e7b4075a9aef992406e18f5",
      "statement": "Dense embedding failure is a degradation, not a read failure: convergence completes the lexical/graph catch-up and advances the checkpoint when the embedder is absent or errors, and retrieval fuses only the channels that answered while reporting `dense_used=False` with a reason, so the dense channel is optional at runtime and partially embedded batches leave real vectors rather than zero placeholders.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/hypermnesic/converge.py#L147-L168",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc24ec2217eed9558e57f2d79803a36d06362a8fbf873c26d7163e689214116d:"
