    {
      "id": "claim_df3fccc924ad4f13916017eb8706baed",
      "statement": "Every artifact that mutates the corpus flows through one of two gated write shapes — a direct guard-checked `commit_note` call, or the review-gated proposal queue (`propose.py`) which emits a path-scoped, gate-checked commit on a `hypermnesic/proposals/<slug>` branch surfaced as a PR the owner approves and which is never auto-merged, reusing the same guard, gate, and audit primitives rather than a parallel write path.",
      "evidence": [
