    {
      "id": "claim_cb3151b76e6d448a80485f145245c798",
      "statement": "Documentation drift is an architectural rule: a change is not done until every document it affects is corrected in the same PR (MCP tool surface, CLI, configuration, write guard, auth topology, retrieval/convergence each have named docs), changes to `serialize.py`, `frontmatter_gate.py`, `auth*.py`, and `mcp_server.py` are security-sensitive and CODEOWNERS-routed (requiring `SECURITY.md` and the threat model to move with them), and the pins in `docs/README.md` win over conflicting process-history documents.",
